0 On rock, bark or wood0111502
0 On soil or detritus on soil, usually arctic-alpine011260143
0 Thallus, when fully developed, with apothecia, which may be sometimes with poorly developed hymenium and superficially soralium-like; additionally soralia or isidia may be present0213703
0 Thallus normally without apothecia; soralia, isidia or nodulose excrescences mostly present02148090
0 Ascospores dark at maturity ("Melanaria")0335904
0 Ascospores persistently colourless (Pertusaria s.str.) or ascocarps usually absent03361008
0 Ascospores 1/ascus, c. 150-240 x 50-90 µm04571105
0 Ascospores 2-4/ascus, smaller04581206
0 Ascospores 160-240 x 60-90 µm, finally completely greenish grey; thallus whitish grey, smooth, more or less rimose-areolated, areoles 1-2.5 mm wide; fertile warts not clearly differentiated, discs punctiform, black, to 40/areole; on rock, E Pyreneans, Corsica, Macedonia 0579130 P. spilomantha Nyl.0
0 Ascospores c. 150-180 x 50-70 µm, pale brown, with reticulate striae;. thallus pale grey, continuous, warty; thallus P-, K-, C-, KC-, UV-; indet. fatty acids; apothecia becoming crater-like, lecanorine, abundant and confluent, basally constricted, 1-2 mm diam.; disc lilac-brown, flat to concave, white-pruinose; on Quercus tree base in Spain 05710140  P. sp. 2 (Giralt 1996)0
0 Apothecia in more or less clearly delimited, basally constricted, 1-2 mm wide fertile warts; discs dense, united in discs of 2nd order surrounded by thalline margin; thallus thick, brownish grey, rimose-areolated; norstictic, gyrophoric, connorstictic acids; ascospores 110-160 x 45-95 µm; Greece 06811150 P. pentelici J.Steiner0
0 Apothecia not in fertile warts or in poorly delimited fertile warts; thallus grey, grey-whitish or sometimes creamy white068121607
0 Thallus granularly papillose, scabrid, more or less rimose-areolated, 1-1.5 mm thick; papillae semiglobose, about 0.1 mm wide and high; discs with 2-5 together, immersed; ascospores 96-160 x 50-85 µm, with thick, colourless wall and dark, K+ violet content; on rock, Canary Islands 071213170 P. urceolaria Nyl.0
0 Thallus smooth to rugulose, more or less rimose-areolated, often granular with isidia-like, fragile, c. 0.1 mm diam. papillae leaving sorediate scars; thallus K+ orange-red, with norstictic acid; discs with several together, immersed, with slightly open, brownish black, very irregular and much divided discs; ascospores grey- or olive-black, K+ violet, 2(-4) per ascus, c. 80-100 x 55-85 µm, outer surface minutely pitted; on siliceous rock, Western Europe, ?South Tyrol 071214180  P. lactescens Mudd0
0 Apothecia when fully developed with distinctly widened discs, not perithecium-like086151909
0 Apothecia persistently perithecium-like, with punctiform discs (ostioles), one or several in each fertile wart0861620047
0 Fertile warts soralium-like, with granularly laciniate, more or less sorediate margin and granularly pruinose discs, often with degenerated hymenium; ascospores 1-2/ascus, often poorly developed09151721010
0 Fertile warts not soralium-like, with smooth, not pruinose or slightly mealy, initially often punctiform discs; ascospores 1-8/ascus09151822033
