0 Thallus with norstictic acid and sometimes? with salazinic, fatty acids and xanthone, rather thick, more or less grey, warty-papillose, the warts with sorediate openings; fertile warts to about 1.5 mm wide with 1-4 blackish discs; ascospores 1/ascus, about 100-300 x 50-100 µm; Mediterranean-Atlantic, from Wales and Ireland to Greece; primary species of P. excludens 0132325290  P. monogona Nyl.0
0 Thallus with norstictic and picrolichenic acids, areolated, areoles 0.2-0.5 mm wide; fertile warts 1-1.8 mm wide, prominent, with 1-3 discs, soralia-like; disc black with white pruina; ascospores 1/ascus, 100-150 x 35-50 µm, with strongly striate wall; on siliceous rock near Tanger, also in Spain (Boqueras 2000); primary species of P. teneriffensis 0132326300 P. ludovicae Werner0
0 Thallus without isidia, sometimes with soralia, more or less grey, K- or K+ brownish; fatty acid iH; on sandstone in border area Saxony/Bohemia/Silesia 0142227310  P. ocellata (Wallr.) Koerb.0
0 Thallus without isidia and soralia, K- or K+ brownish; protocetraric acid; on siliceous stone in the Aegean, Greece 0142228320  P. pseudoparotica Sipman0
0 Thallus with coralloid isidia or with columnarly elongated warts014222933015
0 Thallus with dense, columnar, often fertile warts015293034016
0 Thallus with scattered isidia or thallus warts015293135017
0 Thallus with numerous dense, columnar fertile warts occasionally apically bearing 2-5 discs, mostly apically bursting and producing soredia; fatty acids iH; Ireland 0163032360 P. polythecia (Tayl.) Erichsen0
0 Thallus with numerous dense, 2-3 mm high and wide, columnar fertile warts apically bearing 2-4 black-brown discs, at first with greyish cover; ascospores 1/ascus, about 200 µm long; Spain 0163033370 P. clementeana Müll.Arg.0
0 Isidia thin, about 0.1-0.3 mm thick, granular to coralloid, concolorous with thallus, pale greyish to whitish; thallus P+ yellow-orange, K+ yellow, C-, KC-, UV-; thamnolic acid; discs rare, usually in groups of 2-4 in 1.5-2 mm wide fertile warts; discs more or less brown; ascospores 2/ascus, about 80-140 x 40-80 µm; widely distributed and often frequent on boulders and outcrops of non-calcareous rock, occasionally on bark, rather variable; syn. P. subdubia 0173134380  P. corallina (L.) Arnold0
0 Isidia thicker, like thallus warts017313539018
0 Thallus smoky grey, with mammose, about 1-1.5 mm wide, dense, more or less sorediate papillae; thallus P+ red, K+ yellowish to brownish; fumarprotocetraric with or without succinprotocetraric acids; discs rare, 1-2 together on the papillae, with blackish discs; ascospores 180-200 x 60-70 µm; southern France to N. Africa; looks similar to the corticolous P. graeca (28c) 0183536400  P. mammosa Harm.0
0 Thallus without sorediate papillae, grey to smoky grey, with short-cylindrical, 0.4-1 mm wide isidia; thallus P+ red, K+ yellowish to brownish; fumarprotocetraric, tr. protocetraric acids; fertile warts more or less semiglobose, usually with 1-4 blackish discs; ascospores 1/ascus, of very variable size; on rock poor in lime, in the Carpathians, variable 0183537410  P. stalactiza Nyl.0
0 Thallus without isidia or soredia, pale grey, thick, coarse-wartily areolated; thallus warts basally constricted, to 3 mm high, with somewhat worn-off surface, centrally depressed; fumarprotocetraric, succinprotocetraric acids; apothecia immersed in warts, with black discs; spores unknown; central Italy 0183538420  P. etrusca Erichsen0
