0 Thallus not K+ yellow turning red; norstictic acid absent019204044023
0 Spores 2/ascus; thallus without sorediate excrescences; apothecia with grey-pruinose discs; ascospores about 120-150 x 60 µm; Greece 0203941450  P. rhodiensis Erichsen0
0 Spores 1/ascus; thallus with sorediate excrescences020394246021
0 Thallus yellowish white to brownish, with irregular, sorediate excrescences; apothecia immersed, with black discs; ascospores about 30-80 x 20-40 µm; Finland 0214243470  P. atropallida Vain.0
0 Thallus grey, without or with regular sorediate excrescences021424448022
0 Thallus thin, long remaining endophloeodic, covered with numerous whitish-sorediate, 0.6-1 mm wide, convex warts, which partly bear a single blackish, white-pruinose disc; ascospores 200-300 x 50-100 µm; France 0224445490  P. monogoniza Nyl.0
0 Thallus epiphloeodic, often granular-warty, thin, not rimose, more or less grey; fertile warts flat, almost of lecanorine appearance, usually with a single, widely open, black, usually pruinose disc; ascospores about 70-150 x 25-40 µm; rare in humid sites in Bavaria 0224446500  P. waghornei Hulting0
0 Thallus (medulla) K+ yellow, P+ yellow to orange, thin, more or less endophloeodic, grey to whitish; thamnolic acid; fertile warts numerous, about 1 mm wide, with usually a single reddish disc; ascospores (1-)2/ascus, (38-)94(-160) x (18-)36(-58) µm, often not well developed; rare in western and central Europe; syn. P. laevigata (Nyl.) Arnold 0234047510  P. trachythallina Erichsen0
0 Thallus K- or K+ indistinctly yellowish or brownish023404852024
0 Thallus C+ red; fertile warts of lecanorine appearance, with usually a single reddish disc 0244849530 see P. velata 44a0
0 Thallus C-024485054025
0 Ascospores 2/ascus, about 100-150 µm long; thallus whitish, rimose to radiate-plicate; thiophaninic acid, sometimes with confluentic and/or 2'-O-methylperlatolic acid; fertile warts to 1 mm wide, usually with several (-8) dark discs; thallus K and P almost -; Mediterranean 0255051550  P. ilicicola Harm.250
0 Ascospores 1/ascus025505256026
0 Discs reddish; thallus P+ red or at least KC+ pink or violet, not orange026525357027
0 Discs grey to black; thallus P-, KC- or KC+ orange026525458029
0 Medulla KC+ violet; thallus P- but soralia P+ orange-red to red; picrolichenic acid; fertile warts strongly convex, usually with a single brownish disc; ascospores about 220-350 µm long; thallus usually without soralia; on deciduous trees in Central Europe, more common in the Mediterranean; status uncertain, seems distinct in Mediterranean but is usually synonymized elsewhere; syn. P. amara var. slesvicensis 0275355590  P. slesvicensis Erichsen0
0 Medulla KC+ pink; thallus P+ orange-red to red; picrolichenic acid absent027535660028
0 Thallus rather thick, shelf-like areolate, bluish grey; physodalic, tr. protocetraric acids; fertile warts white, usually with a single, reddish disc; ascospores about 90-200 µm long; on smooth bark, often Fagus or Abies, in subatlantic parts of western Europe, extending to the Baltic Sea and the northern Alps; syn. P. leptospora Nitschke 0285657610  P. multipuncta (Turner) Nyl.0
0 Thallus rather thick, more or less rimose-areolated; fertile warts little emergent, with 1-5 small, (pale- to) dark brown discs; ascospores about 150-230 µm long; thallus K+ reddish, P+ deep yellow, the warts P+ orange; atlantic part of Central Europe, rarely found; =P. multipuncta? 0285658620  P. laureri Erichsen0
0 Thallus whitish grey with strong, 0.5-1 mm wide papillae and apothecium-like, 1.5-3 mm wide fertile warts and - sorediate warts; discs usually several together, to 1.5 mm wide; ascospores about 160-280 x 50-80 µm; fertile warts and medulla P+ red; fumarprotocetraric with + succinprotocetraric or protocetraric acids; several times found in Greece, Sardinia, Corsica; looks like corticolous form of P. mammosa 0285659630  P. graeca Erichsen0
0 Thallus KC-, UV-, fatty acids029546064030
0 Thallus KC-, UV-, no substances present; ascospores about 200 m long; thallus epiphloeodic, pale ashy grey, finely rimose-areolate; fertile warts about 1 mm wide, with a single blackish disc; Italy, Crete 0295461650  P. cf. rhodiensis Erichsen0
0 Thallus KC+ pink, UV-, fumarprotocetraric acid;  discs dark-brown or black, level to sunken, c. 0.4 (0.1-0.87) mm wide, usually single, initally white-pruinose, later pruinose-sorediate to sorediate; ascospores cylindric, (66-)134(-196) x (21-)46(-69) mu;  reported from Spain (Boqueras 2000) 0295462660 P. multipunctoides Dibben0
0 d Thallus KC+ orange, UV+ orange-red, thiophaninic with planaic or confluentic acids029546367032
0 Medulla J+ blue; thallus thin, at first endophloeodic, smooth to warty; thallus K, C and P-; fertile warts to over 1 mm wide with a single, deeply immersed, blackish disc; ascospores about 90-140 µm long; so far only near Gdansk, on Betula; =P. ophthalmiza?? 0306064680 P. brachyspora Erichsen0
0 Medulla J-030606569031
0 Thallus flat, not areolated, thin to rather thick, not sorediate; fertile warts more or less regularly distributed, flat, 0.5-1 mm wide, usually with 1-2, greyish pruinose to blackish, to 0.5 mm wide discs; ascospores about 130-200 x 50-70 µm; 4 indet. fatty acids; on leached bark of e.g. Betula and Abies in oceanic and mediterranean areas, in particular in mountain forest 0316566700  P. ophthalmiza (Nyl.) Nyl.0
0 Thallus verrucose, not areolated, rather thick, sorediate; rarely fruiting, with scattered, about 1-4 mm wide fertile warts 0316567710 see P. albescens 141b0
0 Thallus not sorediate; thiophaninic, planaic, 4-O-dimethylplanaic acids; fruits lecanorine with black disc more or less covered with thick, white pruina; epithecium greenish, K+ violet; ascospores 120-190 x (40-)60-75(-90) µm; on Juniperus in continental Spain 0326368720  P. paramerae Crespo & Vezda0
0 Thallus more or less sorediate, brownish white, more or less rimose; thiophaninic, confluentic acids; hymenium 400-500 m high; fertile warts in dense groups, to about 1 mm wide, with blackish disc and swollen thalline margin; ascospores about 150-250 x 60-90 µm; Greece 0326369730  P. corinthiaca Erichsen0
0 Thallus not sorediate, whitish, granular-warty-rimose; thiophaninic, 2'-O-methylperlatolic acids; fertile warts appressed, with a single blackish disc covered by white pruina composed of several apothecia; hymenium 250-300 µm; ascospores about 180-220 x 75-100 µm, with thick, smooth wall; Mediterranean 0326370740   P. caesioalba (Flot.) Nyl.0
0 (9) Ascospores (6-)8/ascus, usually under 50 µm long033187175034
0 Ascospores 4/ascus, about 30-60 x 25-35 µm; discs blackish; paraphyses simple to little branched; thallus whitish, P-, with dense, almost semiglobose fertile warts; no substances; on soil or bark; syn. P. freyi Erichsen 0331872760Megaspora verrucosa (Ach.) Hafellner & V.Wirth0
